,"body":"Plan-review PASSED (verdict PASS, 0 blocking; signed at ae203145f). Acting on advisories:\n- E2 (detail-line format unspecified): pinning a concrete, testable format — new lines as `  new       <file>::<symbol> score=<n> threshold=<15>` and increased lines as `  increased <file>::<symbol> score=<n> ceiling=<c>`, stable-sorted by key within each group, printed after the unchanged summary line.\n- E4 (dropped, but accurate): the terse-output contract is documented by the module 'Exit-code contract' docstring + tests/unit/test_complexity_baseline.py::test_help_documents_contracts, NOT ADR 0058 (that ADR governs the module-size LOC ceiling). Implementation/docs will cite the docstring/test, not ADR 0058, to avoid propagating the misattribution.","timestamp":1787956681350330001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented under RED->GREEN. render_violation_details() added and wired into _run_check; summary line unchanged, additive detail lines only on failing check; Exit-code contract docstring updated. 87/87 unit tests pass; make lint (exit 0) and make typecheck (Success) green; ruff C901 on the script clean; --check baseline still passes (active=39 new=0 increased=0 stale=10). Pushed to Gerrit as change 2349 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2349), commit 4fbca3fe77ad with rebar-ticket trailer + DCO. Awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 before Submit + close.","timestamp":1787956990556935001}],"created_at":1787955861751727001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8a688241-239e-4674-9741-daffe4271561","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"0ab0-6754-cc72-4d8c"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` prints only aggregate counts on a failing check (e.g. `active=41 new=2 increased=1 stale=7`). It never names the offending symbols, their files, current McCabe scores, or the baseline ceiling/threshold they breached. Diagnosing a CI failure (e.g. Gerrit run 32914110990) currently requires a separate local no-cache Ruff census plus manual baseline comparison — especially poor in resource-constrained CI-only workflows. Split out from bug 0ab0-6754-cc72-4d8c, which the operator classified not_a_bug: the terse output is the documented, --help-surfaced, unit-tested contract (ADR 0058), so this is an approved ENHANCEMENT, not a defect.\n\n## Plan\n- Preserve the existing compact counter summary line (`active=<A> new=<N> increased=<I> stale=<S>`) byte-for-byte so anything parsing it today keeps working.\n- On a FAILING `--check` (new>0 or increased>0), after the summary emit additive, deterministic per-symbol detail lines:\n  - one line per `new` symbol naming file::symbol, its current McCabe score, and the configured threshold (COMPLEXITY_THRESHOLD = 15).\n  - one line per `increased` symbol naming file::symbol, its current score, and its recorded baseline ceiling.\n- Detail lines are stable-sorted (by key) and grouped deterministically.\n- Keep passing and stale-only output compact — NO detail lines when there is no regression.\n- Do NOT alter the pass/fail gate logic (has_regression / exit codes) — formatting only over already-computed data; scanner/gate runtime unchanged.\n- Update the module \"Exit-code contract\" docstring and test_help_documents_contracts if new tokens are surfaced in --help.\n- Add focused unit coverage for detail values, ordering, and absence-on-pass.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A failing `--check` names every `new` symbol with file::symbol, current score, and the allowed threshold.\n- [ ] A failing `--check` names every `increased` symbol with file::symbol, current score, and baseline ceiling.\n- [ ] Detail lines are stable-sorted and appear together with the existing summary line, which is unchanged.\n- [ ] A passing or stale-only check retains compact output with no violation detail lines.\n- [ ] Pass/fail gate logic and exit codes are unchanged.\n- [ ] Focused tests plus `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py","reason":"Render deterministic additive per-symbol new/increased violation detail lines on a failing --check."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_complexity_baseline.py","reason":"Cover violation detail values, ordering, and compact passing/stale output."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"6b109e1e-e710-41cb-88f8-a45c5d2d0542","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"75e0-d630-90ca-4580","ticket_type":"task","title":"Diagnostics: surface per-symbol detail on complexity-baseline --check failure","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["650f5c56-c8a9-44c8-bc0d-c24f8f7c11f6","8a688241-239e-4674-9741-daffe4271561","c25f0f75-5ed6-4053-b72d-bcf7b7812a7f","48b84fa0-6df8-4368-9b0f-e3da462336d3","6b109e1e-e710-41cb-88f8-a45c5d2d0542","fbfe8006-f20b-4080-8e7d-f35a91dd191f","fa7173e3-63d6-4069-bbcb-50a67fbba4b1","2d8b9675-267d-4fa1-a0d9-4f432465c38d"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787956990556935002,"uuid":"92cdc9bf-d90f-4022-a279-3763b371ec38"}